# /simulate-budget (Cursor Command Rule)

When the user asks to simulate runner memory, check for OOM risks, or triggers `/simulate-budget`:

1. Run the simulation script:
   ```bash
   python3 .agents/skills/gitlab-ci-optimizer/scripts/simulate_budget.py [flags]
   ```
   Supported flags:
   - `--stack <node|python|go>`
   - `--ram <MB>` (e.g. 1024, 2048, 4096)
   - `--vcpus <count>` (e.g. 2)
   - `--slots <count>` (concurrent runner slots)
   - `--workers <count>` (test processes per job)
   - `--shards <count>` (parallel test jobs)

2. Evaluate the output:
   - If `OOM_KILL (Exit 137)`: Warn the user and calculate the maximum safe workers (`<= floor((RAM*0.75 - BASE) / PER_WORKER)`).
   - If workers > vCPUs: Recommend capping workers to vCPUs to prevent CPU thrashing.
   - If shards > slots: Recommend reducing shards to prevent queueing in waves.
